--------------------------------------------------------
System Requirements:
--------------------------------------------------------
  IBM 386 PC or 100% compatible, VGA graphics card
  2 Megs of RAM
  21 Megs free on the hard disk
  Microsoft 100% compatible mouse and driver
  MSDOS 5.00 or later

Recommendations:
  Sound Blaster or 100% compatible sound card
  Windows 95

--------------------------------------------------------
Troubleshooting (Win 95 only):
--------------------------------------------------------
  The best way to run this game under Win95 is by using
  a shortcut.  When setting up the shortcut be sure to
  set the memory options as shown below.

  How to create a shortcut under Win95.
    Right click on the desktop
    Select NEW
    Select shortcut
    Browse for (SW.BAT)
    Click on NEXT
    Enter a name to be displayed under the icon
    Click on FINISH
    Once your shortcut has been created, 
       make the following changes:

    Select the 'Program' Tab
    Set Cmd line to run SW.BAT
    Set Working to TYRANTS directory
    Check the 'close on exit' box
    Select the 'Misc' Tab
    Foreground 'uncheck' Allow screen saver
    Select the 'Memory' Tab
    Set all options to Auto
    Select 'Apply'

  
  If you are using a Sound Blaster compatible or if you
  have a non-standard Sound Blaster installation, you
  must insure that the "BLASTER" environment variable
  is properly set.  You can open a DOS window and type
  "SET".  What you see displayed are the environment
  variables, if there is not a "BLASTER=", you can add 
  it to the AUTOEXEC.BAT file.  Be sure to use the 
  proper values for your sound card.

      Example:
	 SET BLASTER=A220 I5 D1 H5 P330 E620 T6

--------------------------------------------------------
Troubleshooting (DOS and Win 3.x):
--------------------------------------------------------
  Your system must either load EMM386 or another memory
  manager that provides access to EXPANDED memory.  The
  program requires a minimum of 2 Megs, but will use up
  to 8 Megs if it is available.
      CONFIG.SYS Example:
	 DEVICE=C:\DOS\EMM386.EXE RAM

  Your mouse driver must be loaded prior to running the
  game.  This is normally done in the AUTOEXEC.BAT file.

  If you are using a Sound Blaster compatible or if you
  have a non-standard Sound Blaster installation, you
  must insure that the "BLASTER" environment variable
  is properly set in the AUTOEXEC.BAT file.
      Example:
	 SET BLASTER=A220 I5 D1 H5 P330 E620 T6

  If your system does not use the standard Sound Blaster
  FM driver (SBFMDRV) you will need to modify the batch
  file (SW.BAT) to load the proper driver.

  In all cases, the BLASTER environment variable is
  required for proper sound operation.

  If you run this software under Windows and experience
  problems, run the game in a "pure" DOS environment.

